(7229737, 1115554, 19959, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>This is an interesting flower, not one that I recognise..<br/> <br/>It is just about sharp enough in the right places to work, although it might have benefited from a little more DOF.<br/> <br/>It didn''t score well in this challenge and although it didn''t pick up any DNMC comments I''m sure the low voters<br/>had this in mind when scoring... i.e. Unless it screams "Park" it will suffer in the votes.<br/> <br/>I hope the challenge encouraged you to go out into your local park and look for shots with your camera... which is one<br/>of the aims of the community.. <br/> <br/>Chris<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club... This is an interesting flower, not one that I recognise.. It is just about sharp enough in the right places to work, although it might have benefited from a little more DOF. It didn''t score well in this challenge and although it didn''t pick up any DNMC comments I''m sure the low votershad this in mind when scoring... i.e. Unless it screams "Park" it will suffer in the votes. I hope the challenge encouraged you to go out into your local park and look for shots with your camera... which is oneof the aims of the community..  Chris', '2014-06-17 09:18:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7229738, 1114825, 19959, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>Interesting shot and certainly meets the challenge. Well done for seeking out and composing for the symmetry of the refection.<br/>It is sometimes hard to find a photograph in the every day (which is what made this challenge a hard one to participate in. I didn''t submit an entry!)<br/> <br/>There is a old piece of photography advice that states. ''Frame the shot how you feel is right. Then take a step further forward and take the picture''<br/>This is good advice a lot of the time and will really help add impact to your shots.. give it a go next time you are out and about.<br/> <br/>This image needs a little more impact IMO. I''d even go as far as cropping the top and bottom and making the aspect Landscape...<br/>It did not score that high, perhaps because the park element although present is not the main subject element.<br/> <br/>Chris<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club... Interesting shot and certainly meets the challenge. Well done for seeking out and composing for the symmetry of the refection.It is sometimes hard to find a photograph in the every day (which is what made this challenge a hard one to participate in. I didn''t submit an entry!) There is a old piece of photography advice that states. ''Frame the shot how you feel is right. Then take a step further forward and take the picture''This is good advice a lot of the time and will really help add impact to your shots.. give it a go next time you are out and about. This image needs a little more impact IMO. I''d even go as far as cropping the top and bottom and making the aspect Landscape...It did not score that high, perhaps because the park element although present is not the main subject element. Chris', '2014-06-17 09:25:10.000000', NULL, 0),
